# interplay_lifetime_placement_after_delete: With a placement list (opcode 68; the service with argument buffers only, docs/testing.md section 6.11) a buffer made with a zero entry writes its GPU address there. DeleteResource (37) zeroes the entry, and the buffer made again by the next exec writes an address again. The addresses are the host's: a relation kernel (fixtures/shaders/rel.metal) compares the entry before the delete with zero and the entry after the re-creation with zero, so only "nonzero" is locked; the entry between is dumped (all zero). A buffer over the placement list's own page reads the entries on the GPU.
